{#-
  The destination body: the authored sections, the record's host, basis and witnesses shown
  in a `## Provenance` section, and the workaround's cost (its cost lines) and the contributing
  locations each collapsed. It shows no estimate line: the priority, estimated from the record's
  `impact`, is the destination's own field. Given every variable README.md's "Templates"
  documents.
-#}
{%- set impact = ticket.section("Impact") -%}
{%- set fix = ticket.section("Suggested fix") -%}
## Root cause

{{ ticket.section("Root cause").content }}

## Provenance

- Host: {{ record.host }}
{% for origin, commit in record.basis | items -%}
- Basis: {{ origin }} at {{ commit }}
{% endfor -%}
{% for witness in record.witnesses or [] -%}
- Witness: {{ witness }}
{% endfor %}
## Impact

{% for part in impact.parts if part.label != rubric.impact_parts[-1] -%}
**{{ part.label }}.** {{ part.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% for part in impact.parts if part.label == rubric.impact_parts[-1] -%}
{{ collapsed(part.label, impact.lines | selectattr("label", "in", rubric.workaround_costs) | map(attribute="text") | join("\n")) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- for section in ticket.sections if section.name not in ["Root cause", "Impact"] %}
## {{ section.name }}

{% if section.name == "Suggested fix" -%}
{{ section.lead }}
{% for part in section.parts if part.label == "Contributing locations" %}
{{ collapsed(part.label, part.text) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- for subsection in section.subsections %}
### {{ subsection.heading }}

{{ subsection.content }}
{% endfor %}
{%- else -%}
{{ section.content }}
{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
